From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 21:53:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove hosted account CLI commands

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Remove hosted account management and device authorization from the CLI.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1011-personal-feature-disable-automatic-onboarding.patch

Patch intent:
Remove the account subcommand, browser device-login command path, and account
management implementation from the CLI while preserving normal provider flags
and ordinary API-key configuration.

Why it exists:
A local build must not expose hosted account, billing, activation, or device
authorization workflows as command-line functionality.

Upstream integration points:
The patch removes the account CLI module, device authorization implementation,
command parsing, login dispatch, process title mapping, and parser coverage.

Update guidance:
Do not restore hosted account commands or browser device authorization. Keep
direct provider and OpenAI-compatible API-key configuration available through
the existing CLI options.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode hosted_account_subcommand_is_not_available --lib
